{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Everything's ready except credentials. Here's what I found and what I propose.\n\n**The PR's claim:** Triton defaults fp32 `tl.dot` to TF32; PyTorch reference has TF32 off → backward gradients diverge (~0.72 max diff), failing `atol=5e-3`. Fix adds `input_precision=\"ieee\"` to 9 sites.\n\n**The thing that makes this worth actually testing:** your README says these tutorials were tested and pass on an RTX 4060 Ti — which is Ada and *also* has TF32. If Triton unconditionally defaulted to TF32, your 4060 Ti runs should have failed too. So either the reporter's Triton 3.1.0 differs from your pinned 3.2.0, their env differed, or something else is going on. That's the crux I want to settle empirically. Your README also notes the 3090 gives \"incorrect values\" — possibly the same root cause, which this PR might actually fix.\n\n**Test matrix I'll run** (same instance, no extra cost): `main` vs PR branch × repo-pinned env (torch 2.6.0 / triton 3.2.0) vs reporter's env (torch 2.5.1 / triton 3.1.0), plus `TRITON_F32_DEFAULT=ieee` on `main` as a control.\n\nLive vast.ai prices (queried just now, search works without auth):\n\n| GPU | arch | cheapest reliable | why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| RTX 4090 | Ada | **$0.295/hr** | exactly matches PR author's claim |\n| RTX 3090 | Ampere | **$0.113/hr** | \"older\" card your README flags as bad |\n| RTX 2080 Ti | Turing | **$0.069/hr** | true pre-TF32 hardware — strongest regression check |\n| RTX 4070 | Ada | $0.069/hr | cheap Ada substitute for the 4090 |\n\nDocker images confirmed available for both env combos.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/deprecated/triton_docs_tutorials","dirty_fingerprint":"126c4977a00f41293cb34f75913ba953e022e70c8c3a3d7a5586ae0036745547","head":"1d79d23423ffb9f2853dddbeb22aabb82dca8af8","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/triton_docs_tutorials.git"},"id":"ev2-95dca03c8a90974c5251a36b5506ab2f8074322550e1bbc