{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Your `~/.ssh/id_ed25519_vastai.pub` is there — once I'm authenticated I can register it with vast myself via the CLI, so you don't need to touch SSH.\n\nTwo things I need from you:\n\n**1. A vast.ai API key.** Log in with GitHub at https://cloud.vast.ai/manage-keys/ (Account → API Keys), create/copy a key, then run it in this session so it never lands in my transcript output:\n\n```\n! ~/.local/bin/vastai set api-key YOUR_KEY_HERE\n```\n\n**2. Confirm the account has credit** — vast needs a positive balance to rent. ~$5 covers this several times over.\n\n**Plan once authenticated:** I'll rent the 2080 Ti ($0.069/hr), 3090 ($0.133/hr), and 4090 ($0.310/hr) **in parallel** rather than sequentially — same total GPU-hours, but ~45 min of wall clock instead of ~2.5 hrs, so roughly **$0.40 for all three**. That leaves plenty of headroom to add the 5090 ($0.366/hr) afterward. Well under your $5 cap.\n\nOn each: `main` vs PR #7 vs `main` + `TRITON_F32_DEFAULT=ieee` (control), 4 test configs each, cold Triton cache every run. Then on the 4090 I'll additionally rebuild the reporter's exact stack (torch 2.5.1 / triton 3.1.0) to check whether this is version-specific to Triton 3.1 vs your pinned 3.2.\n\nOne flag on the 5090: it's Blackwell `sm_120`, which torch 2.6/triton 3.2 cannot compile for at all, so that one necessarily tests a newer stack (torch 2.7+/triton 3.3+) rather than your pinned versions. Still a useful \"does the fix hold on current hardware\" data point, just answering a slightly different question.\n\nneeds input: vast.ai API key set via `! ~/.local/bin/vastai set api-key YOUR_KEY`, plus confirmation the account has credit.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/deprecated/triton_docs_tutorials","dirty_fingerprint":"126c4977a00f41293cb34f75913ba953e022e70c8c3a3d7a5586ae0036745547","head":"1d79d23423ffb9f2853dddbeb22aabb82dca8af8","repo":"git@github.com:evintunad